      "body": "Closes the declarations half of #1936 (remainder 2; the wantlog half landed separately). Task 19664.\n\n## What\n\nThree shipped example API declarations in `pkgs/mcpx/examples/`, in the same form as the landed `tailscale.json`:\n\n- `dropbox.json` + `dropbox.openapi.json` — Dropbox API v2 reads: listFolder, listFolderContinue, getMetadata, searchFiles, getCurrentAccount.\n- `google-drive.json` + `google-drive.openapi.json` — Drive API v3 reads: listFiles, getFile, getAbout, listDrives.\n- `outlook.json` + `outlook.openapi.json` — Microsoft Graph v1.0 reads: listMessages, getMessage, listMailFolders, listEvents, getProfile.\n\nEach declaration points at a curated OpenAPI document shipped beside it: the vendor documents are unusable as published (Drive publishes a discovery document, Dropbox a Stone spec, Graph's document covers all of Microsoft 365), so each shipped document is a small read-only subset — the thinnest wrapper, per the issue's Approach B item 5.\n\n## Decisions (recorded on #1936 before authoring)\n\n- Credential model: exactly one header per declaration, `Authorization: Bearer ${VAR}` with the placeholder expanded from the environment by mcpx (`DROPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_DRIVE_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `OUTLOOK_ACCESS_TOKEN`). A declaration can be checked in; a token cannot.\n- Dropbox sets `methods: [\"POST\"]` deliberately — API v2 is RPC over POST, and every declared operation is a read. Drive and Outlook declare GETs only, so the read-only default applies.\n- No write, upload, download, send or delete operation is declared for any service.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `TestShippedAPIDeclarations` (`internal/cli/api_shipped_test.go`, the `adapter_shipped_test.go` pattern): each declaration loads via `loadAPIFiles`, carries exactly the one placeholder bearer header, and its document loads and builds (`openapi.Load`/`Build` with the declaration's own options) to exactly the pinned tool set.\n- `go test ./internal/cli/ ./internal/config/ ./internal/openapi/ -count=1` — all pass on the laptop.\n- Docs: a parallel section beside the tailscale example in `docs/configuration.md`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797498908&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11171&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11171&signature=0bb95a694772caea49f9a2fbf3d5c1fa56a1118da5d5c197ea9a87f3fee4a557\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/11171?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
