      "body": "The #1936 best item (queue task 3233): a doctor check built from evidence mcpx already collects.\n\n## What changed\n- New `internal/cli/doctor_remote.go`, wired into `CmdDoctor`:\n  - For each configured **remote (url)** server, aggregates the log store's per-tool call stats (`logstore.Calls`) into per-server figures: calls, errors, error rate, and the slowest tool's p95.\n  - Gates (stated in the code, not tuned in secret): volume floor **50 calls**; slow at **p95 ≥ 500ms** or **error rate ≥ 5%**. Above the floor and slow → a `remote latency` warning naming the server, its URL, and its measured numbers.\n  - Only for a flagged server, the registry is asked (same client/settings as `/v1/registry/search`) whether an entry under that exact name carries an installable package; if so the fix recommends local hosting with the package (`mcpx registry add <name> --write` installs …). Registry failure costs the recommendation, never the report.\n  - **Read-only**: the check builds check rows and nothing else; it never edits config.\n- Tests (`doctor_remote_test.go`) cover the four named cases — slow remote with a local package (recommendation fires, numbers named), slow remote without one (report only), local command server (never flagged, even with terrible stats), low-volume remote (silent below the floor) — plus the per-tool→per-server aggregation.\n\n## Tests (laptop)\n`go test ./internal/cli/ -run 'TestSlowRemote|TestLocalCommand|TestLowVolume|TestAggregateRemote'` — all pass. Full `go test ./...` runs in CI.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/2597?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img al