        "merged_at": "2026-11-02T16:03:20Z"
      },
      "body": "Slice 1 of #1933 (Approach B, per triage task 2829): declared `toolViews` on alias (`aliasOf`) views. This PR references #1933 and does **not** close it — slice 2 (cross-server virtual namespaces) stays there.\n\n## What\n\n- **config** — `mcpx.toolViews` map on a server's extras: each entry names a target tool via `from` (rename), may `pin` fixed arguments, may `hide` pinned properties, and may override `description`. Structural validation at resolve: toolViews requires `aliasOf`, `from` is required, and `hide` may only list pinned properties.\n- **Listings** — a non-empty toolViews map IS the view's allowlist: `visibleTools` materialises exactly the named tools under their view names (sorted, deterministic), with the description override applied and hidden properties removed from the exposed `inputSchema` (`properties` + `required`). Unrenamed `tools`/`excludeTools` behaviour is unchanged for servers without toolViews.\n- **Calls** — `resolveAndGuard` translates a view call to the target's real name with pinned arguments merged over the caller's (a pin wins), so the write policy, the destructive floor, the pool, and history/diagnostics all work with the real name and the effective args, on every call path (`Call`, `CallReporting`, `CallAsk`). The target's real name is not callable through the view (`VisibleTool` answers in view names).\n- **Load validation** — when the target's schemas are cached, registry load rejects an unknown `from` target or a pin of an argument the target schema does not declare, naming the server and view.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe tailscale shape from #1933 end to end at the daemon level: an alias view exposing exactly `listTailnet` (from `list_tailnets`) and `listHostnames` (from `list_devices`, `tailnet` pinned to `-` and hidden) — listings, schema hiding, pin merging (caller cannot override), guard behaviour (view name passes, real name is HiddenTool), plus config resolve/visibility and validation tests.\n\nVerified on the laptop worktree: `go test ./internal/config/ ./internal/daemon/` — both pass in full. CI is the remaining verification.\n\nQueue task 3230 · issue #1933 (stays open for slice 2)\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/2976?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796022100&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=2976&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F2976&signature=224cef8dc273ff29e76865843cd64fcfe68bd458910c2a37d518892385e8e663\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Create named tool views for aliases with custom descriptions, hidden pinned properties, and preset arguments.\n  * Views appear under their configured names, and pinned values take precedence over caller-supplied values.\n  * Advertised schemas reflect pinned arguments and relevant requirements, dependencies, and constraints.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Calls through views use the target tool and merged arguments when applying policies and invoking the tool.\n  * Configuration parsing preserves precise numeric values and rejects trailing or additional JSON documents.\n* **Validation**\n  * Invalid tool views are rejected during configuration resolution or registry updates.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
